Z||000000||SteveJ||11-29-2001||11:02 PM||||I also own a Caddy so I visit their sites. This site has some interesting info on Northstar engine failures. I think if you are going to use one of these in a Fiero you want the overflow tank as high as possible. <P>Also Cadilac sells some tablets to be dropped in the coolant when it is changed. You wouldn't want to forget them.<BR> <A HREF="http://members.home.net/gtrose/" TARGET=_blank>http://members.home.net/gtrose/</A> ||||reg||8
Z||000001||artherd||11-30-2001||12:03 AM||||Sounds like BS to me.<P>First, although the starter is in the vee, it is actually VERY easy to get to. <P>Second, the secondary torque strut is attached to the coolant crosover tube, NOT to the water pump.<P>I know of two people with over 200k miles on their N* cars (both Eldorados)  They've changed plugs and coolant.  Once.<P>Good note about electrolsis though, I'll install some head-block-head grounding straps, just to be safe.<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>(PS: yes, 100kmiles is recomended intervals on both)<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000002||Formula88||11-30-2001||12:15 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by artherd:<BR><B>Sounds like BS to me.<P>First, although the starter is in the vee, it is actually VERY easy to get to. <P>Second, the secondary torque strut is attached to the coolant crosover tube, NOT to the water pump.<P>I know of two people with over 200k miles on their N* cars (both Eldorados)  They've changed plugs and coolant.  Once.<P>Good note about electrolsis though, I'll install some head-block-head grounding straps, just to be safe.<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>(PS: yes, 100kmiles is recomended intervals on both)<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Good points, Ben.  But attaching a torque strut to the coolant crossover tube doesn't sound too swift either.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Still, I'm sure someone will have a bad experience with any car.  If we relied on bad press to make our decisions, who here would have bought a Fiero?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||KissMySSFiero||11-30-2001||01:12 PM||||i didnt read the stuff at the link but i worked at a cadi dealer for a year as a mechanic.  one thing.  great engine.  the only major problem we had was the head gaskets leaked.  it was always the front one.  which makes it easy to fix in a front engine car.  and that was rarely on  a car with less than 100k miles.  the starter is less than an hour job once you know the trick.  all you do is hold up the intake with a block.   you dotn have to remove any fuel lines, coolant lines, etc.  just a few bolts a block of wood and your at the starter.  i wouldnt hesitate to put a N* in any car except for the cost.  <P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:SSFiero <BR>88FORMULA<BR>       <A HREF="mailto:SSFiero@Aol.com">SSFiero@Aol.com</A>        <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||northstarfieroorbust||11-30-2001||07:08 PM||||Ahh, i plan on putting a N* in my fiero asap, so if you guys haven any good sites, input, recommendations, whatever(as long as it has to do with N* and the fiero) im all ears.  Please email me, thanks||||reg||14
Z||000005||SteveJ||11-30-2001||07:31 PM||||I think you have to learn from other people's problems. I don't think that freezes you into inaction or allows you to be dismissive.<P>So you read the problems these guys experienced and you take action that it doesn't happen to you. You put the tablets in the coolant, easy on the headbolt torque, ect.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Jay||11-30-2001||07:41 PM||||Northstarfieroorbust, I love the name!  I haven't experienced any of these problems with my Fiero Northstar.  It has been reliable and fun for the last two years However a friend of mine has it in his caddy and the head did leak, and was misdiagnosed by GM.  Now he has a warped head and GM wants over $2000 to do it!  I got him a new engine from a 99 for $1300Canadian.<P>In case you haven't heard, my car is for sale on ebay, check link below! <A HREF="http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=598567222" TARGET=_blank>http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=598567222</A> <P>------------------<BR>Jay<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/newsig2_copy_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
